    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP is headlined today by **Corbin Carroll**, who boasts our highest efficiency score of 85.94. His matchup against Javier is an ideal scenario; the combination of a favorable SP skill rating, the +8% boost from batting second, and the green light provided by the pitcher's slow delivery makes him a lock for a multi-category impact, particularly in our priority category of stolen bases. **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **Brice Turang** (75.06) follow closely behind. Both are buoyed by \"slow-to-the-plate\" opposing pitchers, providing them with the highest probabilistic upside for theft today, while **Turang** also benefits from a favorable wind projection that further solidifies his standing as a top-tier play.\n\nOur most difficult selection decision landed on the bench, where **Cole Young** (47.13) narrowly missed the final cut behind **Zach McKinstry**. While **Young** possesses decent matchup indicators against Morris, his base projection was ultimately cannibalized by a negative park factor and a lack of the specific situational upside\u2014such as stolen base potential or a high-leverage order spot\u2014that allowed **McKinstry** to maintain a higher floor despite his own bottom-of-the-order penalty. We are also exercising caution with **Austin Riley** (40.59) today; facing a high-caliber arm like S\u00e1nchez against a left-handed pitcher makes him a defensive sit to preserve game caps, as his efficiency drops below our threshold for a standard start.\n\nThe rest of the squad provides solid, reliable production, with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.70) and **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) serving as anchors against favorable matchups where their platoon edges remain intact. We are keeping a close watch on **James Wood**; while his 52.21 score is somewhat tempered by an elite opposing pitcher in Snell, his xwOBA remains too dangerous to bench. We are betting that his elite underlying talent and leadoff spot will overcome the lack of a favorable pitcher matchup, keeping him in the mix as we push for gains in our 5x5 categories.",
